      },
      "rationale": "Any other request first tests the reader-moved guard (`selectionFocusAvailable`). A `scrollOnly` request (a refresh) only brings the selected node into view, with `block: 'nearest'`, and moves no focus. Any other request calls `focusSelectedRead`, which for a kept-tree selection focuses the selected row with `preventScroll` and reveals that row inside its own panel at either width; the former stacked-layout center reveal is not part of the current handler.",
      "role": "enforcement"
